1
00:00:15,529 --> 00:00:19,368
<i>SAWYER FARM
ESTABLISHED 1845

2
00:00:20,994 --> 00:00:30,048
<i># Happy birthday to you...

3
00:00:30,172 --> 00:00:35,013
<i># Happy birthday, dear Jed...

4
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:39,934
<i># Happy birthday to you...

5
00:00:40,059 --> 00:00:41,771
All right, now make a wish.

6
00:00:41,806 --> 00:00:42,773
Blow them out.

7
00:00:47,568 --> 00:00:49,821
Yes! Very good!

8
00:00:49,862 --> 00:00:52,032
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

9
00:00:52,073 --> 00:00:53,284
Very good!

10
00:00:53,408 --> 00:00:54,702
All right...

11
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:00,586
Drayton, where are your manners?

12
00:01:00,669 --> 00:01:02,838
Give the first slice to the thief.

13
00:01:17,605 --> 00:01:19,086
I didn't steal your damn pigs...

14
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:20,568
Are you calling my son a liar?

15
00:01:20,693 --> 00:01:22,946
He saw your filthy hands stealing our property...

16
00:01:27,532 --> 00:01:30,329
Why would I go anywhere near your filthy pigs?

17
00:01:30,453 --> 00:01:31,915
Or your filthy family!

18
00:01:31,998 --> 00:01:35,085
I swear, everybody will know what kind of...

19
00:01:35,126 --> 00:01:37,004
...offspring you're raising here, Verna!

20
00:01:37,086 --> 00:01:38,923
Shut him up! I've had enough!

21
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,433
Listen to me, no farmhand is going to...

22
00:01:42,468 --> 00:01:44,264
...ruin my son's special night.

23
00:01:47,517 --> 00:01:48,894
Ready for your present?

24
00:01:52,189 --> 00:01:54,192
You know you're my special boy.

25
00:01:54,775 --> 00:01:56,862
Come on, Jed. There you go...

26
00:01:59,699 --> 00:02:01,952
- Jed.
- Yes, that's it, Jed.

27
00:02:04,455 --> 00:02:05,499
Now remember,

28
00:02:05,707 --> 00:02:08,836
bad people like him try to destroy our family.

29
00:02:09,461 --> 00:02:11,256
But we won't let that happen, will we?

30
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:12,798
Go on, pick it up...

31
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:15,093
Jed, pick it up...

32
00:02:15,634 --> 00:02:16,470
Jed!

33
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:20,223
Jed...

34
00:02:20,264 --> 00:02:21,810
Pick it up, Jed!

35
00:02:21,851 --> 00:02:25,147
Jed!

36
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:27,941
Come on, you know what you have to do...

37
00:02:28,358 --> 00:02:30,071
That's it, Jed!

38
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:33,491
Come on, Jed...

39
00:02:34,199 --> 00:02:37,037
Jed!

40
00:02:37,119 --> 00:02:38,580
No!

41
00:02:38,621 --> 00:02:39,874
There you go.

42
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,542
Go on, son!

43
00:02:41,577 --> 00:02:42,878
No!

44
00:02:49,592 --> 00:02:51,304
No!

45
00:02:56,894 --> 00:02:58,981
No!

46
00:02:59,147 --> 00:03:00,983
No, please!

47
00:03:01,108 --> 00:03:03,903
No!

48
00:03:03,944 --> 00:03:06,573
Do it, do it, do it!

49
00:03:06,614 --> 00:03:08,575
No!

50
00:03:08,616 --> 00:03:10,327
Go on, Jed, do it...

51
00:03:11,286 --> 00:03:12,330
Do it!

52
00:03:12,914 --> 00:03:15,126
- Jed.
- Do it!

53
00:03:21,423 --> 00:03:22,551
Mom!

54
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,594
Mom, no!

55
00:03:26,346 --> 00:03:29,685
No!

56
00:03:39,571 --> 00:03:40,406
Hey.

57
00:03:40,697 --> 00:03:42,284
You let us down, Jed.

58
00:03:45,036 --> 00:03:48,123
It's all right. Family will always be here for
you.

59
00:03:48,289 --> 00:03:49,624
Remember that.

60
00:03:50,375 --> 00:03:51,418
All right.

61
00:04:09,106 --> 00:04:14,197
<i>TEXAS, 1955

62
00:04:17,198 --> 00:04:18,619
Are you trying to get us killed?

63
00:04:18,659 --> 00:04:19,536
Do you want me to stop?

64
00:04:19,578 --> 00:04:20,829
No, I didn't say that.

65
00:04:28,130 --> 00:04:29,216
Watch out!

66
00:04:33,929 --> 00:04:35,725
What the hell was that thing?

67
00:04:37,016 --> 00:04:38,228
Hey, Betty.

68
00:04:45,443 --> 00:04:46,695
What is it?

69
00:04:47,987 --> 00:04:49,115
I don't know.

70
00:04:52,368 --> 00:04:53,830
Then let's go.

71
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,092
What?

72
00:05:12,476 --> 00:05:13,812
He's just a kid!

73
00:05:15,856 --> 00:05:17,150
Let's go!

74
00:05:17,524 --> 00:05:18,943
We'll be late.

75
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,572
Hello.

76
00:05:26,828 --> 00:05:28,122
Are you okay?

77
00:05:34,253 --> 00:05:36,298
You shouldn't play in the road.

78
00:05:36,464 --> 00:05:38,425
Help me, please...

79
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,561
Hey, Betty, where are you going? I didn't hit him!

80
00:05:46,977 --> 00:05:48,605
- Something's wrong.
- Betty!

81
00:05:48,645 --> 00:05:50,065
He needs help.

82
00:05:50,607 --> 00:05:52,025
Jesus Christ!

83
00:05:56,447 --> 00:05:58,409
Hey, buddy, can you hear me?

84
00:06:00,411 --> 00:06:01,954
Let me help you!

85
00:06:05,832 --> 00:06:07,001
Hello?

86
00:06:13,633 --> 00:06:16,222
It's okay. You can come out.

87
00:06:17,679 --> 00:06:18,808
Betty.

88
00:06:22,603 --> 00:06:24,314
Betty, where did you go?

89
00:07:22,594 --> 00:07:23,889
Hello?

90
00:07:29,061 --> 00:07:32,607
Come on... I won't hurt you.

91
00:07:35,150 --> 00:07:36,653
I just want to help...

92
00:07:43,703 --> 00:07:44,872
Okay?

93
00:07:55,761 --> 00:08:00,058
<i>BASED ON CHARACTERS CREATED BY

94
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:03,104
<i>KIM HENKEL AND TOBE HOOPER

95
00:08:05,397 --> 00:08:07,441
You did good, Jed!

96
00:08:08,233 --> 00:08:11,279
It's like... I can still feel you in there
after all.

97
00:08:42,607 --> 00:08:46,196
Well, let him learn a little more.

98
00:08:49,657 --> 00:08:51,202
Oh, my God!

99
00:09:00,838 --> 00:09:01,757
Show him!

100
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:16,357
- Where is she?
- Calm down, Hal.

101
00:09:16,857 --> 00:09:18,444
Let me through, damn it!

102
00:09:18,485 --> 00:09:20,030
Let me go! Let me go, damn it!

103
00:09:20,070 --> 00:09:21,655
- We know what happened.
- Calm down, Hal.

104
00:09:21,821 --> 00:09:23,450
Is that my little girl in there?

105
00:09:24,951 --> 00:09:27,830
Is she in there? Is my little girl in there?

106
00:09:28,164 --> 00:09:29,541
Answer me, damn it!

107
00:09:29,874 --> 00:09:31,251
We've got one of them.

108
00:09:35,630 --> 00:09:37,009
Oh, boy!

109
00:09:41,179 --> 00:09:42,557
I couldn't get to her in time!

110
00:09:42,765 --> 00:09:44,810
I'm so sorry, sir. I swear to God.

111
00:09:47,311 --> 00:09:49,022
Drayton Sawyer...

112
00:09:51,524 --> 00:09:53,403
It's time to go to Gorman Reformatory.

113
00:09:53,444 --> 00:09:56,783
No... You're all grown up now.

114
00:09:59,034 --> 00:10:01,038
That means the gas chamber for you.

115
00:10:04,708 --> 00:10:05,962
Why?

116
00:10:06,294 --> 00:10:08,131
Are you going to arrest me for finding a dead
body?

117
00:10:08,338 --> 00:10:09,800
Last I checked, that wasn't a crime.

118
00:10:09,849 --> 00:10:12,603
How about a bullet hole in your damn skull?

119
00:10:13,269 --> 00:10:14,569
- Put it away, Hal.
- Come on.

120
00:10:14,604 --> 00:10:16,482
He's right. We've got nothing on him...

121
00:10:16,856 --> 00:10:18,065
Calm down, Hal.

122
00:10:18,273 --> 00:10:19,025
Keep your head clear.

123
00:10:19,065 --> 00:10:21,569
- Hal, it's not worth it.
- Come on, Hal, lower the gun.

124
00:10:21,693 --> 00:10:23,029
Damn trash.

125
00:10:34,205 --> 00:10:36,166
Let those boys go right this instant!

126
00:10:36,457 --> 00:10:38,126
Don't count on it, Verna!

127
00:10:38,876 --> 00:10:40,337
Do you think they did anything wrong?

128
00:10:40,377 --> 00:10:41,463
No, I don't!

129
00:10:41,545 --> 00:10:43,381
You bastard, let them out of the car!

130
00:10:43,881 --> 00:10:46,676
No! They're going to stay there and rot!

131
00:10:47,759 --> 00:10:48,844
On what charges?

132
00:10:49,135 --> 00:10:50,429
They're not under arrest.

133
00:10:50,470 --> 00:10:52,765
They're in protective custody... from you.

134
00:10:52,806 --> 00:10:54,058
What are you talking about?

135
00:10:55,058 --> 00:10:57,603
I can't count how many crime scenes I've been
to...

136
00:10:57,644 --> 00:10:59,981
...where there's always a Sawyer involved.

137
00:11:00,523 --> 00:11:02,316
Those boys aren't safe with you...

138
00:11:02,398 --> 00:11:03,526
Bullshit.

139
00:11:04,442 --> 00:11:06,780
Get a warrant for the Sawyer house.

140
00:11:07,112 --> 00:11:09,157
Name every one of them. I want them all.

141
00:11:09,323 --> 00:11:10,325
- Did you hear me?
- You can't do that.

142
00:11:10,407 --> 00:11:11,284
You can't do that!

143
00:11:11,367 --> 00:11:13,078
Well, by the time we get there, I'll have a
warrant saying I can...

144
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:14,621
...do just that.

145
00:11:15,287 --> 00:11:17,414
It's called "children at risk."

146
00:11:18,832 --> 00:11:20,793
You took one of mine...

147
00:11:21,543 --> 00:11:23,963
...so I'll take every one of yours, Verna.

148
00:11:30,135 --> 00:11:31,511
Every last one of them...

149
00:11:33,513 --> 00:11:35,516
<i>10 YEARS LATER

150
00:11:35,974 --> 00:11:39,645
<i>In 1935, the state of Texas established a...

151
00:11:39,686 --> 00:11:42,189
<i>...program to care for children at risk.

152
00:11:42,355 --> 00:11:45,693
In its first year, nearly 52 children were
removed from homes...

153
00:11:45,774 --> 00:11:48,611
...known to be involved in criminal activity.

154
00:11:48,944 --> 00:11:51,824
<i>Many of these children were given new names...

155
00:11:51,865 --> 00:11:53,659
<i>...and placed in foster homes.

156
00:11:53,783 --> 00:11:57,371
<i>Others, products of degenerate parenting...

157
00:11:57,412 --> 00:12:00,249
<i>...ended up here at Gorman Reformatory.

158
00:12:00,290 --> 00:12:01,665
<i>GORMAN HOUSE JUVENILE REFORMATORY

159
00:12:01,706 --> 00:12:05,836
We take care of their physical and
psychological needs.

160
00:12:06,294 --> 00:12:07,547
Yes, sir.

161
00:12:07,671 --> 00:12:10,467
I've wanted to come here for a long time.

162
00:12:10,757 --> 00:12:12,093
I think I can help them.

163
00:12:12,259 --> 00:12:13,303
Elizabeth.

164
00:12:13,343 --> 00:12:14,971
Please, sir, Lizzy. Lizzy is fine.

165
00:12:15,012 --> 00:12:16,513
Elizabeth.

166
00:12:17,472 --> 00:12:19,725
Most of these children will end up...

167
00:12:19,765 --> 00:12:21,977
...in prisons or mental institutions.

168
00:12:23,019 --> 00:12:26,483
Keeping them here makes everyone safer.

169
00:12:27,274 --> 00:12:28,526
Keep your guard up.

170
00:13:13,194 --> 00:13:14,571
Well... hello...

171
00:13:15,404 --> 00:13:16,865
My name is Lizzy.

172
00:13:16,948 --> 00:13:19,827
I'm new here, and I'd like to get to know you.

173
00:13:24,372 --> 00:13:25,707
That's Bud.

174
00:13:27,333 --> 00:13:29,709
He doesn't say much for such a big guy.

175
00:13:35,132 --> 00:13:36,134
You're in my seat.

176
00:13:36,675 --> 00:13:37,844
I'm sorry.

177
00:13:38,718 --> 00:13:40,721
- Very nice.
- I'm...

178
00:13:40,762 --> 00:13:42,807
Lizzy... Yeah, I heard. I heard.

179
00:13:43,806 --> 00:13:45,976
Shit, sorry. I'm Jackson.

180
00:13:46,767 --> 00:13:49,730
Jackson and... Bud...

181
00:13:50,522 --> 00:13:52,984
And what medication are you taking, Jackson?

182
00:13:53,150 --> 00:13:54,360
Medication?

183
00:13:55,569 --> 00:13:57,530
They already gave it to us when they brought
us in, right?

184
00:13:58,529 --> 00:14:01,449
We figured you'd know more about that than we
do, Lizzy...

185
00:14:02,449 --> 00:14:04,871
You're not going to give me any trouble, are you?

186
00:14:05,370 --> 00:14:06,831
No, not me, Lizzy.

187
00:14:08,165 --> 00:14:09,464
Is there a reason you keep...

188
00:14:09,499 --> 00:14:11,043
...saying my name like that?

189
00:14:11,626 --> 00:14:15,880
No... I just like to know who's in charge,
that's all.

190
00:14:18,965 --> 00:14:20,635
Fuck you, asshole!

191
00:14:20,676 --> 00:14:21,595
I'll kick your ass.

192
00:14:21,635 --> 00:14:23,388
I'll fuck up your head!

193
00:14:23,512 --> 00:14:24,598
Let him go!

194
00:14:24,638 --> 00:14:26,183
Mind your own business!

195
00:14:26,307 --> 00:14:27,690
It is my business.

196
00:14:27,725 --> 00:14:29,143
What's the problem?

197
00:14:29,642 --> 00:14:32,062
He said something I didn't like.

198
00:14:32,353 --> 00:14:35,858
About what a girl in a nurse's uniform would
taste like.

199
00:14:36,733 --> 00:14:38,320
Hey, hey, let go of me!

200
00:14:38,611 --> 00:14:39,988
Let go!

201
00:14:40,821 --> 00:14:42,407
Fuck you, Frankenstein!

202
00:14:42,448 --> 00:14:44,074
That's enough. Stop it.

203
00:14:44,449 --> 00:14:46,870
- Ike, what did you do?
- I didn't do anything.

204
00:14:49,914 --> 00:14:51,124
Everything's fine.

205
00:15:52,099 --> 00:15:53,726
What are you doing?

206
00:15:58,688 --> 00:15:59,982
Come here.

207
00:16:03,318 --> 00:16:04,821
What's the problem?

208
00:16:04,862 --> 00:16:06,698
It's just a stupid mouse.

209
00:16:09,575 --> 00:16:10,869
Got a light?

210
00:16:10,951 --> 00:16:12,786
You know smoking isn't allowed in here...

211
00:16:15,079 --> 00:16:17,458
I have special permission.

212
00:16:18,250 --> 00:16:19,502
True story.

213
00:16:19,543 --> 00:16:21,463
Ask Dr. Lang.

214
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:22,505
I will.

215
00:16:22,546 --> 00:16:24,507
He'll tell you it helps me.

216
00:16:25,591 --> 00:16:28,217
With my anxiety.

217
00:16:31,470 --> 00:16:33,014
The truth is...

218
00:16:34,055 --> 00:16:36,185
...it's because I'm his favorite.

219
00:16:36,559 --> 00:16:38,021
He told me so.

220
00:16:38,228 --> 00:16:40,898
- You've earned yourself a warning.
- Why?

221
00:16:40,938 --> 00:16:42,483
I was just taking a bath.

222
00:16:42,523 --> 00:16:43,859
Get out.

223
00:16:47,278 --> 00:16:48,572
Bitch.

224
00:16:50,406 --> 00:16:52,160
Is everything all right?

225
00:16:52,868 --> 00:16:55,079
Yes, Doctor, I'm fine.

226
00:16:55,661 --> 00:17:00,542
I'll handle Isaac and Bud.

227
00:17:00,625 --> 00:17:02,377
No. Bud didn't do anything.

228
00:17:02,418 --> 00:17:04,817
I look forward to our session tomorrow, Jackson.

229
00:17:04,852 --> 00:17:07,216
I'm sorry, but he's actually right.

230
00:17:07,256 --> 00:17:08,551
Bud didn't do anything.

231
00:17:08,592 --> 00:17:10,718
He was fighting...

232
00:17:11,343 --> 00:17:13,012
Well, he was protecting me...

233
00:17:13,094 --> 00:17:14,347
Remind me to tell you later what...

234
00:17:14,387 --> 00:17:15,973
...he did to his last foster family.

235
00:17:16,056 --> 00:17:17,725
Well, they took his dog away.

236
00:17:18,266 --> 00:17:21,562
Yes... that's a perfectly good reason...

237
00:17:21,603 --> 00:17:24,232
...to put someone in a coma.

238
00:17:24,607 --> 00:17:26,108
Well, I'm just saying.

239
00:17:48,546 --> 00:17:49,464
<i>DIAGNOSIS: BIPOLAR DISORDER

240
00:17:49,505 --> 00:17:53,426
<i>Upon admission, this 16-year-old boy,
Horton, Bud, was depressed, agitated and
fearful.

241
00:17:53,551 --> 00:17:56,594
<i>Overall, his behavior was aggressive,
unusually energetic and withdrawn.

242
00:17:59,806 --> 00:18:01,642
Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

243
00:18:02,392 --> 00:18:03,727
You didn't.

244
00:18:04,477 --> 00:18:06,063
Thank you for helping Bud.

245
00:18:07,147 --> 00:18:10,775
I know you don't even know him, so that was nice.

246
00:18:11,525 --> 00:18:14,445
Well, I'm here to help you all. So...

247
00:18:16,197 --> 00:18:18,492
You're the first pretty nurse we've had around
here.

248
00:18:21,369 --> 00:18:22,955
So I thought you should know...

249
00:18:24,456 --> 00:18:25,624
Know what?

250
00:18:25,957 --> 00:18:28,587
What goes on in the relaxation room...

251
00:18:29,503 --> 00:18:31,382
The kids around here call it...

252
00:18:31,548 --> 00:18:33,801
...Dr. Lang's chamber of horrors.

253
00:18:34,217 --> 00:18:35,803
Piece of shit.

254
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,638
Why is that?

255
00:18:38,013 --> 00:18:40,514
Go there at night and find out for yourself...

256
00:18:42,056 --> 00:18:44,560
Hey, you might even do something about it.

257
00:18:45,935 --> 00:18:47,021
You know.

258
00:18:48,189 --> 00:18:49,316
Jackson...

259
00:18:51,609 --> 00:18:53,777
You'll get out of here one day.

260
00:18:54,068 --> 00:18:56,697
And just because you can't trust certain people...

261
00:18:58,198 --> 00:19:00,326
...doesn't mean you shouldn't trust others.

262
00:19:01,409 --> 00:19:03,037
Well, I'll think about it.

263
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:09,919
<i>DR. LANG

264
00:19:14,506 --> 00:19:16,008
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

265
00:19:16,090 --> 00:19:18,761
Barry Farnsworth, we had an appointment an
hour ago.

266
00:19:18,843 --> 00:19:20,262
Did we?

267
00:19:22,556 --> 00:19:24,098
Mrs. Sawyer.

268
00:19:24,264 --> 00:19:26,434
It's Mrs. Carson now.

269
00:19:32,523 --> 00:19:34,108
I want to see Jed.

270
00:19:34,441 --> 00:19:36,528
We've been through this before.

271
00:19:37,027 --> 00:19:38,404
Year after year...

272
00:19:38,445 --> 00:19:39,781
He's my son.

273
00:19:40,197 --> 00:19:41,825
And I can afford a lawyer now.

274
00:19:41,865 --> 00:19:43,868
That doesn't change anything.

